<!-- event-labels: generated by tools/build-mod.py from cards/trees/*.tree.json.
     Do not hand-edit. Appended to vanilla events_boss.xml; last definition wins. -->

<textList name="EVLBL_BOSS_FLEETS_BOTH">
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

Sensors indicate evidence of a huge battle nearby, but the immediate vicinity seems quiet. You try to lay low and keep out of the fighting.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

You arrive to find two fleets crashing against each other. Sensors are tracking the extent of the carnage. You quietly wait for the FTL drive to charge, knowing that the only way you can help is by completing your mission.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

A battle rages in the distance. Sensors suggest the presence of many vulnerable escape pods, but you know you cannot stop to help. The mission is paramount.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

A battle rages on in the distance. As much as you would like to help in the fight, you know the importance of your mission.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

You don't need advanced Sensors to tell there is a battle going on. You look out of the window quietly, waiting to jump. There's no way you can help in this fight.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

Two fleets are volleying shots at each other. Luckily, no one seems interested in your ship. You prepare to make another jump.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

Sensors indicate evidence of a huge battle nearby, but the immediate vicinity seems quiet. You try to lay low and keep out of the fighting.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

You arrive to find two fleets crashing against each other. Sensors are tracking the extent of the carnage. You quietly wait for the FTL drive to charge, knowing that the only way you can help is by completing your mission.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

A battle rages in the distance. Sensors suggest the presence of many vulnerable escape pods, but you know you cannot stop to help. The mission is paramount.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

A battle rages on in the distance. As much as you would like to help in the fight, you know the importance of your mission.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

You don't need advanced Sensors to tell there is a battle going on. You look out of the window quietly, waiting to jump. There's no way you can help in this fight.</text>
	<text>[ Two fleets in battle (Last Stand) ]

Two fleets are volleying shots at each other. Luckily, no one seems interested in your ship. You prepare to make another jump.</text>
</textList>

<event name="BOSS_FLEETS_BOTH">  <!-- nodes that have ships fighting  -  unique background -->
	<fleet>battle</fleet>
	<text load="EVLBL_BOSS_FLEETS_BOTH"/>
</event>

<textList name="EVLBL_BOSS_FLEETS_FED">
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

You arrive to see a number of Federation forward-carriers and dreadnoughts. This must be a system of high importance to warrant such a fleet.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

There are a few Federation fleets in the nearby area as well as a lot of wreckage. There must have been minor skirmishes in the area.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

A few scattered heavy vessels are left to defend the nearby Federation settlement. They seem to be in the process of evacuation.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

A large host of Federation heavy vessels are in formation around the beacon. Sensors run hot with missile locks, but once you transmit your ship signature they leave you alone.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

A battalion of Federation fighters are fighting around a nearby moon with their carriers waiting in the distance. They must have encountered a Rebel scout squadron.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

You arrive to see a number of Federation forward-carriers and dreadnoughts. This must be a system of high importance to warrant such a fleet.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

There are a few Federation fleets in the nearby area as well as a lot of wreckage. There must have been minor skirmishes in the area.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

A few scattered heavy vessels are left to defend the nearby Federation settlement. They seem to be in the process of evacuation.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

A large host of Federation heavy vessels are in formation around the beacon. Sensors run hot with missile locks, but once you transmit your ship signature they leave you alone.</text>
	<text>[ Empty beacon (Last Stand) ]

A battalion of Federation fighters are fighting around a nearby moon with their carriers waiting in the distance. They must have encountered a Rebel scout squadron.</text>
</textList>

<event name="BOSS_FLEETS_FED">  <!-- empty nodes that the Rebels have not reached yet.-->
	<fleet>fed</fleet>
	<text load="EVLBL_BOSS_FLEETS_FED"/>
</event>

<textList name="EVLBL_BOSS_FLEETS_BOTH_FIGHT">
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

You arrive in the middle of a raging battle. Both sides are taking heavy losses. A small squadron flies past and a fighter breaks off, moving toward your position.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

Two fleets fight nearby. You try to skirt around the edges of the battle and keep out of weapons range, but a Rebel scout spots you and moves in.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

It's hard to tell who is winning the nearby battle. Before you have a chance to figure it out, a fighter moves in to attack.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

The sheer scale of the destruction in the distance is almost breath-taking. Unfortunately, your position as an independent observer doesn't last for long!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

The destruction in the distance is almost awe-inspiring. However you're dragged back to reality as Sensors indicate you are under attack.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

You don't have any time to worry about the battle in the distance. The fight is coming to you really quickly!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

You arrive in the middle of a raging battle. Both sides are taking heavy losses. A small squadron flies past and a fighter breaks off, moving toward your position.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

Two fleets fight nearby. You try to skirt around the edges of the battle and keep out of weapons range, but a Rebel scout spots you and moves in.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

It's hard to tell who is winning the nearby battle. Before you have a chance to figure it out, a fighter moves in to attack.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

The sheer scale of the destruction in the distance is almost breath-taking. Unfortunately, your position as an independent observer doesn't last for long!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

The destruction in the distance is almost awe-inspiring. However you're dragged back to reality as Sensors indicate you are under attack.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Federation and Rebel fleets ]

You don't have any time to worry about the battle in the distance. The fight is coming to you really quickly!</text>
</textList>

<event name="BOSS_FLEETS_BOTH_FIGHT">  <!-- nodes that have ships fighting  -  also inside the /!\ symbol but can be elswhere too. -->
	<fleet>battle</fleet>
	<text load="EVLBL_BOSS_FLEETS_BOTH_FIGHT"/>
	<ship load="BOSS_FLEETS_REBEL" hostile="true"/>
</event>

<textList name="EVLBL_BOSS_FLEETS_REBEL">
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

Although you were expecting the Rebels, you never imagined their fleet could have grown so fast. You scanners can hardly register them all before a fighter stationed nearby moves in to attack.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

This system is flooded with Rebel warships. Luckily your ship's signature is disguised as a civilian transport. Most heavy vessels ignore you but a small fighter is approaching with weapons hot!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

You arrive to find a Rebel battalion encircling a nearby planet, launching landing parties. A small scout moves toward your position. Prepare for a fight!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

As soon as you arrive you find yourself in the debris of a fierce battle. However, only Rebel warships remain and you find yourself immediately under attack.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

Shots fly by and your computer registers multiple weapon locks as soon as you arrive. Evasive action!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

What was once a great series of space stations is now nothing but a small ring of debris around the nearby moon. There's no time to mourn the dead; an enemy approaches!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

The Federation seems to have put up a good fight. A number of Rebel ships lie broken or wounded. However their overwhelming numbers force the remaining Federation forces to retreat. Hopefully you can get away in time as well.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

Although you were expecting the Rebels, you never imagined their fleet could have grown so fast. You scanners can hardly register them all before a fighter stationed nearby moves in to attack.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

This system is flooded with Rebel warships. Luckily your ship's signature is disguised as a civilian transport. Most heavy vessels ignore you but a small fighter is approaching with weapons hot!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

You arrive to find a Rebel battalion encircling a nearby planet, launching landing parties. A small scout moves toward your position. Prepare for a fight!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

As soon as you arrive you find yourself in the debris of a fierce battle. However, only Rebel warships remain and you find yourself immediately under attack.</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

Shots fly by and your computer registers multiple weapon locks as soon as you arrive. Evasive action!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

What was once a great series of space stations is now nothing but a small ring of debris around the nearby moon. There's no time to mourn the dead; an enemy approaches!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel fight among Rebel fleet ]

The Federation seems to have put up a good fight. A number of Rebel ships lie broken or wounded. However their overwhelming numbers force the remaining Federation forces to retreat. Hopefully you can get away in time as well.</text>
</textList>

<event name="BOSS_FLEETS_REBEL"> <!-- areas that the fleet took over (or will take over soon) have the /!\ symbol on the map-->
	<fleet>rebel</fleet>
	<text load="EVLBL_BOSS_FLEETS_REBEL"/>
	<ship load="BOSS_FLEETS_REBEL" hostile="true"/>
</event>

<textList name="EVLBL_BOSS_SCOUT_RESCUE">
	<text>[ Rebel ship attacking civilians in Last Stand ]

Shots fly by your port windows followed by a Rebel scout in pursuit of a damaged cruiser. Should we move in to engage?</text>
	<text>[ Rebel ship attacking civilians in Last Stand ]

There seems to be a small Federation colony under attack by a Rebel forward scout. Will you protect them?</text>
	<text>[ Rebel ship attacking civilians in Last Stand ]

A number of large transports are being pursued by a Rebel bombing squadron. One bomber has managed to slip through the defensive fire, and is poised to wreak havoc among the enormous yet vulnerable transports. There's time for you to advance and take it out!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel ship attacking civilians in Last Stand ]

A battle rages nearby between small fighters; apparently fighting over a space station. The Federation appears to be losing ships fast. Shall we assist them?</text>
	<text>[ Rebel ship attacking civilians in Last Stand ]

A civilian ship is broadcasting a request for assistance on a secure Federation channel. They are being harassed by Rebel scouts. Will you respond?</text>
	<text>[ Rebel ship attacking civilians in Last Stand ]

A number of large transports are being pursued by a Rebel bombing squadron. One bomber has managed to slip through the defensive fire, and is poised to wreak havoc among the enormous yet vulnerable transports. There's time for you to advance and take it out!</text>
	<text>[ Rebel ship attacking civilians in Last Stand ]

A battle rages nearby between small fighters; apparently fighting over a space station. The Federation appears to be losing ships fast. Shall we assist them?</text>
	<text>[ Rebel ship attacking civilians in Last Stand ]

A civilian ship is broadcasting a request for assistance on a secure Federation channel. They are being harassed by Rebel scouts. Will you respond?</text>
</textList>

<event name="BOSS_SCOUT_RESCUE">  <!-- player rescues weakened fed/civilian ship from a rebel scout - fight with rescue-->
	<text load="EVLBL_BOSS_SCOUT_RESCUE"/>
	<choice>
		<text id="event_BOSS_SCOUT_RESCUE_c1_choice"/>
		<event>
			<text id="event_BOSS_SCOUT_RESCUE_c1_text"/>
			<ship load="BOSS_SCOUT_RESCUE" hostile="true"/>
		</event>
	</choice>
	<choice>
		<text id="event_BOSS_SCOUT_RESCUE_c2_choice"/>
		<event>
			<text id="event_BOSS_SCOUT_RESCUE_c2_text"/>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>
